Notes
-----

- The 87.92% elapsed-cycle value is the primary whole-kernel HMMA pipeline
  utilization.  The 88.55% active-cycle value excludes periods when the SM is
  inactive.
- Long-scoreboard stalls occupy 2.63% of active-warp cycles, so this profile
  does not indicate a dominant long-latency memory-dependency bottleneck.
- The test program's profiler-injected wall time is not meaningful because NCU
  replays and serializes the launch.  Use gpu__time_duration.sum (13.35 ms).

Raw report
----------

.ncu/reports/v20_swizzle_l2_dram_scoreboard_hmma.ncu-rep

Command
-------

bash ncu_personal.sh --force-overwrite \
  --export .ncu/reports/v20_swizzle_l2_dram_scoreboard_hmma \
  --target-processes all --launch-skip 1 --launch-count 1 \
  --metrics gpu__time_duration.sum,lts__t_sector_hit_rate.pct,dram__bytes_read.sum,dram__bytes_read.sum.per_second,smsp__warp_issue_stalled_long_scoreboard_per_warp_active.pct,smsp__average_warp_latency_issue_stalled_long_scoreboard.ratio,sm__pipe_tensor_op_hmma_cycles_active.avg.pct_of_peak_sustained_elapsed,sm__pipe_tensor_op_hmma_cycles_active.avg.pct_of_peak_sustained_active \
  ./v20/FP16_GEMM_TensorCore_test 8064 10752 8192 1 1


